{"id": "EUVD-2026-81756", "enisaUuid": "cd04b671-ec17-3b20-93af-1353ab650d28", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb/server: call ksmbd_proc_cleanup() on module init failure\n\nWhen a later initializer fails, the unwind chain releases resources\ncreated after procfs and then jumps directly to class_unregister().\nReturning an error from module_init() leaves the proc tree and its\nper-CPU counters allocated.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:59:01", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7d2cd9269b570347e6e2dd24d4b3c1da868bc91d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f43cbe3b58ce989ce420c3bc875d48e7754c8aba"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90163", "GHSA-vh5f-3q2h-6w9g"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "05fe224a-ae3a-38cc-ab86-9af059061123", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b38f99c1217ae04753340f0fdcd8f35bf56841dc <7d2cd9269b570347e6e2dd24d4b3c1da868bc91d"}, {"id": "1878b03f-9922-3a1b-b25e-a6c4350dfa88", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "381d8381-91ea-3257-a56f-d7cf5fb06e25", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "c521509f-82c0-39c0-9cdc-6f9af2695daa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.0"}, {"id": "df1d18f7-c322-3d72-ae78-caaa22d5b652", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b38f99c1217ae04753340f0fdcd8f35bf56841dc <f43cbe3b58ce989ce420c3bc875d48e7754c8aba"}, {"id": "e86d6c28-7ecf-3b3f-a654-8fd0d88d611a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d4de6a1e-66c7-33bc-87af-b932fca28d29", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}